  "residual_model": {
    "scopes": {
      "matched_no_lirf": "departures with a matched ADS-B surface segment at any airport except LIRF (adsb_matched == 1 and airport != LIRF): the residual model's training and prediction scope (exactly v12)",
      "all_no_lirf": "every departure at any airport except LIRF: a blend scope only (unmatched rows there become (1 - w) * v9 + w * adsb_full)"
    },
    "applies_to": "the residual model is exactly v12's (nb feature set, matched rows outside LIRF, weight 1.0); each candidate then blends the result with the full-data learner's prediction, value = (1 - w) * (v9 + residual) + w * adsb_full, on the candidate's blend scope (matched rows outside LIRF, or every row outside LIRF); rows outside both scopes keep v9 exactly. The learner prediction is never a residual feature (v12_v3 showed that a learned stack over-trusts fold-specific predictions).",
